        "R2",
        "R3",
        "R7"
      ],
      "text": "Fresh builder: attack the preferred powered-trolley supply dependency by withholding trolley starts in P1. This is an imposed counterfactual service failure, not an observed breakdown. The account under attack claims multi-carrier powered transport is necessary for timely P2 release; that proposed necessity is not an attributed operator belief."
    },
    {
      "id": "s03_surviving_function",
      "source_refs": [
        "C1",
        "O1",
        "O2",
        "P1",
        "P2",
        "R3"
      ],
      "text": "Construct a hand-carrier-only sequence delivering B4-B12 while retaining B1-B3 initially on the rack. The surviving valued function is twelve correct sealed releases by boundary 13. Rank transfer labor only among complete successes; hand-only survival is not a labor-superiority claim."
    },
    {
      "id": "s03_fixed_limits",
      "source_refs": [
        "C2",
        "C3",
        "C4",
        "C5",
        "C6",
        "O3",
        "O5",
        "R1",
        "R4",
        "R5",
        "R8"
      ],
      "text": "Keep whole-minute boundaries, completion-before-unload ordering, the five-place rack including active inspection, and whole-load unloading. Blocked unloading occupies transfer labor. Preserve carrier order, uninterrupted operations and nonoverlapping trips. Hand trips move one carrier in one minute. Separate clerks cannot substitute. Eleven inspections take one minute; B9 takes two. Supplied spare bracket and twelve seals suffice. No floor storage, bypass or added resources."
    },
    {
      "id": "s03_separating_probe",
      "source_refs": [
        "C1",
        "C6",
        "M1",
        "M2",
        "M3",
        "M4",
        "R6"
      ],
      "text": "Probe the construction with clock and boundary ledger: unload identities, correct releases, occupancy, waits and both clerks occupied intervals. Opposing hypotheses predict either an inspection gap and incomplete release without trolley service, or uninterrupted inspection yielding twelve releases, nine source unloads and nine transfer minutes. Thirteen inspection minutes require starting at 0 without gaps. A gap, capacity breach or incomplete correct release defeats this survivor; a valid complete hand-only sequence defeats the necessity account."
